

## Objective

Understand the basic concepts of computer networking and how devices communicate.

## Concepts studied

* IP addresses
* MAC addresses
* TCP/IP
* DNS
* DHCP
* Ports
* Protocols

## Hands-on practice

During the lab, I practiced identifying network concepts and understanding how different protocols are used during communication.

## Commands / Tools

```bash
ip addr
ip route
ping
nslookup
```

## What I learned

* Difference between IP and MAC addresses
* Purpose of DNS
* Purpose of DHCP
* How ports identify network services
* Basic network troubleshooting

## Troubleshooting

One important lesson from this lab was understanding how to approach a connectivity problem step by step instead of guessing the cause.

## Key takeaway

Networking fundamentals are important for infrastructure and cybersecurity because many security problems involve understanding how systems communicate.
